1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,368
On Mercury, one day lasts two years.

2
00:00:02,883 --> 00:00:06,446
Mercury races around the Sun in just eighty-eight Earth days.

3
00:00:06,446 --> 00:00:07,848
That's one Mercury year.

4
00:00:08,350 --> 00:00:09,665
But it spins slowly.

5
00:00:09,665 --> 00:00:11,440
Once every fifty-nine days.

6
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:14,201
Three spins for every two laps of the Sun.

7
00:00:14,717 --> 00:00:15,853
Put them together,

8
00:00:15,853 --> 00:00:20,525
and sunrise to sunrise takes about one hundred and seventy-six Earth days.

9
00:00:20,525 --> 00:00:22,041
Two whole Mercury years.

10
00:00:22,341 --> 00:00:24,154
Tap like and subscribe for more.

11
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:28,528
Near its closest pass, Mercury's orbit outruns its spin.

12
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:32,268
In some places, the Sun rises, sets, then rises again.

13
00:00:32,783 --> 00:00:34,461
And with nights lasting months,

14
00:00:34,461 --> 00:00:38,846
the ground swings from about four hundred and thirty degrees to minus one eighty.

15
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:40,605
So could you live there?

16
00:00:40,605 --> 00:00:41,964
Full story on the channel.
